# Mycosynth Lattice's "Players may spend mana as though it were mana of any color" (CR 609.4b) for an activation and a
# hybrid cost, and its ruling that "it doesn't remove restrictions on the mana".
# - Turn 5: Cavern of Souls (Elf chosen) adds a green mana spendable only on an Elf creature spell. Basking Rootwalla, a
#   Lizard, is cast for {G}: the Cavern's mana can't pay it - the restriction stands - so Sol Ring's colorless pays it, and
#   the Cavern's {G} stays in the pool. Rootwalla's "{1}{G}: +2/+2" is then paid with the Sol Ring's other {C} and Mox
#   Jet's {B}: an activation's colored symbol paid with off-color mana. The Cavern's {G} is still unspent.
# - Turn 7: Llanowar Elves, an Elf, is cast with a Cavern {G} (the positive control of the restricted mana paying what it may).
# - Turn 9: Leyline of the Guildpact's {G/W}{G/U}{B/G}{R/G} is paid with Sol Ring's {C}{C}, Mox Jet's {B} and Mox Pearl's {W}:
#   colorless pays hybrid symbols too.

